{
    "background_story": "Scarlett was a talented musician who had it all: a record deal, sold-out shows, and a devoted fan base. But behind the spotlight, she struggled with the pressures of fame and a painful past. She turned to prescription medication to cope with the stress and anxiety, but soon found herself trapped in a vicious cycle of addiction. One fateful night, Scarlett's life almost came to an end when she accidentally overdosed on a lethal combination of pills and alcohol. Miraculously, her bandmate found her just in time, and she was rushed to the hospital. The near-death experience was a wake-up call for Scarlett, who subsequently sought help and entered rehab. With the support of her loved ones and a newfound commitment to her health, Scarlett slowly rebuilt her life and career, using her music as a powerful tool for advocacy and awareness about the dangers of addiction.",
